  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason (skewness) is not present in the verbal report. The individual does not mention the probability distribution in terms of favorable vs unfavorable outcomes, nor do they refer to skewness or left-skewness. Instead, the justification focuses on the potential gain and risk tolerance, suggesting a different reasoning process (e.g., expected value or risk preference). The decision reason requires evaluating the probability mass on the favorable side — which is not done in the report. Therefore, the individual did not use the skewness-based decision reason. The comparison of probability weights (20% vs 25%) is not framed in terms of skewness, and no rule based on skewness is applied. Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
